  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c}$ be unit vectors. Suppose $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}=\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{c}=0$ and the angle between $\\vec{b}$ and $\\vec{c}$ is $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Then $\\vec{a}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5jnPC",
      "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mNzPh",
      "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "v0hkj",
      "text": "$\\vec{b}+\\vec{c}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "D8Mlo",
      "text": "$\\pm 2(\\vec{b} \\times \\vec{c})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\overline{\\mathrm{a}} \\perp \\overline{\\mathrm{b}}$ & $\\overline{\\mathrm{a}} \\perp \\overline{\\mathrm{c}}$\nLet $\\overline{\\mathrm{a}}= \\pm \\lambda(\\overline{\\mathrm{b}} \\times \\overline{\\mathrm{c}})$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow|\\overline{\\mathrm{a}}|= \\pm \\lambda|\\overline{\\mathrm{b}} \\| \\overline{\\mathrm{c}}| \\sin \\pi / 6 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\lambda= \\pm 2\n\\end{aligned}$",
